#X text 20 20 u_map -- the map \, and the only file in Cut It that says what a control means. Devices publish named controls on param \; this turns them into the buses and the output devices' cords \, so nothing in e_ or c_ learns that a nanoKONTROL exists. ref/module/map.md, f 58;
#X text 20 165 creation arg 1: the state directory \, the \$3 u_state takes: the recover breadcrumb lives beside the state files. inlet 1: a BPM a tap or the phone set \, from u_tempo: knob 1 is held there until turned through it. outlet 1: the Volca \, selector-prefixed -- notes <n> <v> <d> \, cc <c> <v> \, program <n> \, note <n> <v>. One outlet per output device \, wired in u_root (C-2). outlet 2: c_steps \, what a press on the drum page means -- step \, vel or pad \, <n> <velocity> \, and a drum-page pad's release at velocity 0 -- and the drums destination's <arg> <0-1> \, knobs 2 and 3's last and track-last \, and swing. outlet 3: u_net \, a bang that flips test mode. outlet 4: u_tempo \, what a press of a cell in cut-it-arrangement-page.txt means \, its role: tap. outlet 5: u_song \, the top row's top <1-8> \, and save and revert. outlet 6: c_melody \, the melody destination's <arg> <value>. outlet 7: u_voices \, <arg> <value>. outlet 8: u_perform \, <arg> <value>., f 58;
#X text 700 20 The map is a table \, by page: cut-it-map.txt \, one row per mapping \, four atoms always -- <page> <control> <dest> <arg> \, a page of all being every page's. u_map-lua reads it and looks each control up., f 76;
#X text 1400 20 The allowlist guard is what makes a table acceptable: a row names a destination that must be a literal argument on the route below \, feeding a handler on this canvas \, and never a send. Skip it and nothing fails., f 76;
#X text 2200 20 A row naming a destination not on the route is a real error \, unknown-dest on err. An unmapped control is normal: it is silent on every bus \, and draws nothing (Brendan \, 2026-11-04)., f 62;
#X text 20 1700 Every control goes through the table \, the left and right columns too: u_voices owns the page. A row for the page on show comes first \, then an all row., f 58;
#X text 1080 1700 The lookup is Lua: u_map-lua reads cut-it-map.txt when it is made \, keeps the key's page \, divides each value into 0-1 \, holds a restored knob until it crosses (pickup) \, and looks the control up. A mapped control leaves as five atoms for the route below \; an unmapped one leaves by no outlet \, since only a control the map binds names itself. The rules are u_map.lua \, tested without Pd by test/gate/lua/u_map_test.lua (ref/module/map.md)., f 62;
#X text 2140 1700 C-6: the Lua sends the looked-up row as a list \, and route matches a selector \, so without the list trim every control would take the reject as unknown-dest., f 62;
#X text 20 1930 At load the Lua answers init with a bang on its third outlet \, which shuts the spigot. No bang means it never loaded -- pdlua missing \, or an error in the Lua -- and fail u_map no-lua says so on the screen: every control is dead., f 62;
#X text 1080 1930 Pickup's rules are the Lua's and its clock and files are here: the boot window shuts at 1000 ms \, and the breadcrumb at 2000 says live when the boot follows a recover. Whether a Save left a knobs.txt is the Lua's \, asked as it is made (items 236 \, 239 and 299)., f 62;
#X text 1080 2160 Arg then value \, always: unpack fires right to left \, so the value is in a cold inlet or a gate before the arg triggers., f 62;
#X text 2140 2160 Value destinations are c_mapped instances \, and the scaling lives there: tempo is c_mapped bpm 210 40 \, 0-1 over 40 to 250 BPM. Each draws its own row and passes arg and scaled value on only while live. The transport chain holds no state: it reads back r start and r stop., f 62;
#X text 20 2390 The spigot is the trigger test \, the same three boxes everywhere: a press is non-zero after normalizing and a release is 0 \, so one test serves every surface., f 62;
#X text 1080 2390 The Volca handlers build the selector-prefixed message m_volca expects. C-6, f 62;
#X text 2140 2390 volca-prog uses the value as a gate \, since the program number is the arg: a fader release cannot select a patch., f 62;
#X text 20 2850 The mode bus gives the Lua its key and nothing else: u_voices alone writes it \, a page's name as the selector (ref/module/voices.md)., f 62;
#X text 1080 2850 The page is u_voices' to keep. The table itself is not persisted \, as it is read from the patch folder., f 50;
#X text 2140 2850 map-route: u_perform's controls come in here \, as this file's own lookups do: <dest> <arg> <value> <target> <live>., f 50;
#X obj 720 440 loadbang;
#X obj 720 490 del 1000;
#X msg 720 580 window-shut;
#X text 2140 1930 The screen shows the mapped value \, named for the destination (bpm 157 \, volca-cc41 64) \, not the raw position (item 238) \, and an unmapped control nothing. volca-key and the button destinations draw nothing either (ref/module/map.md)., f 62;
#X obj 3400 3620 loadbang;
