#X text 5420 1800 drum-page: the arg is a grid index \, looked up in cut-it-drum-page.txt \, the table g_grid paints from \, so c_steps gets a step \, a velocity level or a pad and never a cell. A press at the pad's own velocity \, and a release at 0: c_steps acts on a release of a repeat pad only. A row the layout does not hold is a real error \, like unknown-dest. C-8, f 60;
